---
title: Letters
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageType: feature
section: letters
slug: letters
seo:
  description: All of Joel Goodman's newsletter letters, in one place — reflections on higher ed marketing, web design, and whatever else is on his mind.
---

{# Real page for what's usually reached via the rail's slide-out
   overlay (components/slide-panels.njk) — that overlay stays the
   primary way to browse letters, but a direct visit/bookmark/share
   link to /letters/ needs somewhere to land instead of a 404. Reuses
   the exact same list content (components/letter-list.njk) so there's
   one definition of "what the letters list looks like." Same 3-pane
   shell as appearances.njk/speaking.njk (rail | detail | image panel). #}
<div class="content-column">
  <nav class="rail" id="rail-content" aria-label="Site navigation">
    {% include "components/rail.njk" %}
  </nav>

  <main class="detail" id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <button class="detail__tab" id="detail-tab" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="detail-content" aria-label="Toggle details"></button>
    {% include "components/slide-panels.njk" %}

    <div class="detail__content" id="detail-content">
      <div class="detail__slide">
        <header>
          <h1 class="detail__title">Letters</h1>
        </header>

        {# Not .detail__body -- its `a` rule accent-colors inline prose
           links, which fights .letter-list-panel__item's own color
           for these real <a> list rows (unlike appearances.njk's list,
           whose rows are <button>s the rule never touches). #}
        <nav class="letter-list-panel__list" role="navigation" aria-label="Letter navigation">
          {% include "components/letter-list.njk" %}
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>

<section class="image-panel" id="image-panel" aria-label="Cover image">
  <div class="image-panel__slide" id="image-slide">
    <img
      src="/assets/img/letters-hero.jpg"
      alt="Joel Goodman, wearing a straw hat and tinted glasses, standing thoughtfully beside a geometric-tiled wall"
      class="image-panel__cover"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
      sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 50vw" />
  </div>
</section>
